WEBVTT

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.480
Well... That wasn't any 
good at all, Yoigoshi-kun.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:17.760
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.690
Yoigoshi's raid success rate is about 
70% when he's returning with one point.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:21.000
With two points, it's 30%, and he's almost 
never returned with three or more points.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.670
If you can't get points as an anti,

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.830
you need to get a whole bunch of points 
on raids to increase that success rate.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.650
Captain, what about me?

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.650
Oh... Soma, you're...

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.530
You're doing okay. 
Just keep working hard like this.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.300
Huh?

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.830
Hear that?

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.970
And you, Kyohei...

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.640
you focus too much on the catch 
and become a target for a touch.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.420
On the other hand, Shinji, you're too 
cautious. It makes you slow on the catch.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.620
You both need to watch each 
other carefully as you move.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:49.110
Yes, sir!

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.180
I'll follow your lead next time.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.850
Okay. Why don't we try...

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.800
I think Azemichi is still pretty 
rough around the edges, too.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.890
Yeah. But that's fine.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.370
Right now, he's good just 
having fun playing kabaddi.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.940
Why do you space out like that?

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.940
Kyohei and Shinji learned what it's 
like to lose at the winter tournament.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.800
Sorry.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.380
And Yoigoshi-kun has likely experienced 
that on a much higher level.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.040
Is it really that hard?

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.010
When it happens, 
I can't seem to recover well.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.560
There are things only people who know the 
pain of losing can understand.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.260
I'm sorry, but I have no intention of 
deliberately setting Azemichi up to lose.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.390
I feel the same. If you can win, 
that's the best anyway.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.320
Then, why don't you help me win, too?

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.860
It's been six years since 
you scouted me, you know?

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.090
Yeah.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.100
<i>The Match 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hBegins!!!</i>

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:08.310
He's fast and he can take down raiders.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:12.160
Somehow, I just can't see myself 
catching up to the captain.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.420
If you're here to invite me 
to a team, I refuse the offer.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.200
Hello.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.730
C-Captain?

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.930
I thought I'd share some of 
my nikujaga stew with you.

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.710
<i>What's up with this situation?</i>

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.620
How is it? I'm pretty proud 
of how it turned out.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.500
It's good.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.730
I'm so glad.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.960
But, I mean, it really is good.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:43.740
About nationals... What kind of 
people get to go to that world?

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.940
I've never won a single game. 
Maybe it's presumptuous of me to ask...

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.060
The people who get to go to nationals...

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.970
are the people who seriously give 
everything they've got to get there.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.180
That's the kind of thing 
people usually say, anyway.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.030
Huh?

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:07.970
The reality is, I think only a 
handful of geniuses make it there.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:13.480
<b>"Yoigoshi the Unstoppable" Advances to the Final 4!</b>

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.430
And...

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.790
in spite of everyone making a big 
deal out of me being "unstoppable,"

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.480
I only made it to the final four.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.440
When did you start playing kabaddi, Captain?

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.220
It was so long ago, I don't remember now.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.160
Same here.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:25.100
In middle school, a kabaddi 
association reached out to me,

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.160
and I went overseas a number of times.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:28.570
Overseas?

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.640
It's nowhere close to the 
same scale as soccer.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.370
It was an Asia-only tournament.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:37.250
<i>But that still pretty much makes 
him a representative of Japan!</i>

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.070
We got annihilated.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.600
And we'd been pretty confident, too.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.220
There's always someone better.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.010
That's something you come to understand 
completely if you play sports.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:50.220
But you keep playing anyway.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.670
It's no fun if you don't win, is it?

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:56.270
Well, yeah. No one thinks losing is fun.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.270
Everyone wants to stand at 
the very top, if they can.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.370
As kabaddi slowly spreads through Japan,

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.780
I'll win my way to the top with the 
teammates I practiced alongside...

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:10.780
That's the goal that I have 
held within me all this time.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.180
Let's do it through kabaddi.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.800
You wanted it, too, didn't you, Yoigoshi?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.040
Number one in Japan.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.300
I couldn't even beat you.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.380
Was losing the match frustrating?

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.550
Of course it was!

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.300
I'm the one who's frustrated.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.560
Huh?

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.890
It's nothing. Sorry for staying so late.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.400
I'll head off now.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.280
Huh? Okay. Thanks for the food.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.690
Not at all.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:45.870
Hey!

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:48.820
I was running and I happened to see you.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.070
If you train too much, 
you'll wreck your body, you know?

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:53.830
I'm not you.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.200
What did you and Yoigoshi talk about?

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:02.290
Hm? Our dreams and soccer and things...

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:06.770
Didn't I mention it? He said he 
fought with his teammates and quit.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:08.330
Something like that.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:12.290
Getting him to wear a jersey
 was a major struggle.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.200
He said teammates were annoying.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:17.040
A long time ago, you said 
the same thing, Kei.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:22.720
I'd like to have him play in a match once.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.000
A practice match?

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:24.860
Yeah.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.420
Our opponents would have to be...

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:30.960
a school that would play us five-on-five, 
a team without many players.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.540
How about Souwa? They're close to us, right?

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.460
They're a powerhouse school that made 
the Kanto region final four last year.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:38.860
They won't...

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:39.980
Wait.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.490
This year, <i>that</i> guy is captain, isn't he?

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:47.230
So, the guys on the first string 
are headed overseas, huh?

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:49.360
The world team is on a different level.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.430
Next time, I'll be going, too.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:53.010
Ojo!

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:54.880
Hurry up!

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.370
I'm going now, Kei.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.600
Yeah. Go take your beating and come back!

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.430
Was that a friend of yours, Ojo?

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.670
Yeah. We've been friends 
since elementary school.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:06.920
A guy from the second string, huh?

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.310
Kei? Kei!

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:10.780
What is it?

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.920
It's unusual for you to space out like that.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.350
I was thinking about the training schedule.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.790
Your lies don't work on me, Kei.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.900
They're a powerhouse school.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:23.790
And it's not like we don't know them. 
I know it'll make you self-conscious.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.700
That goes for both of us.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:28.300
Masato isn't someone you can
 lower your guard around, is he?

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:29.730
I suppose so...

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.550
I sent him a text just now.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.310
Being on the world team comes in handy, huh?

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.310
We split up so we could fight each other.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.010
He will absolutely accept the invitation.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.560
<b>Maybe 5-on-5...</b>

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.560
<b>I couldn't ask for more.</b>

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:45.190
<i>I couldn't ask for more.</i>

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.820
<b>Souwa High School</b>

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.780
Make your cant louder!

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:54.030
Yes, sir!

00:07:54.030 --> 00:08:01.790
<b>Souwa High School  Kabaddi Team Captain
Rokugen Ayumu</b>

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:57.570
First-years, the tape marking the 
court is starting to come up.

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:59.510
Kabaddi is a sport that carries great risks.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.070
Do not neglect proper maintenance!

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:01.790
Sir!

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.990
Second- and third-years run sprints. Let's go!

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:04.920
Sir!

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:11.820
Ow!

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:17.760
<b>Souwa High School  Kabaddi Team Second-Year
Takaya Ren</b>

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:15.130
Oh, that was a nice sound.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.980
T-Takaya-senpai!

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:21.220
I'll help! Because I'm 
a nice senpai, you see.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.920
Second-years are running sprints, too.  
Don't slip off on your own.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:27.850
Let me hear you!

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:30.030
Yes, sir!

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.030
Yeah...

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:34.240
He may be like that, but he is our 
ace after all... that Takaya-senpai.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.300
You start slacking off as soon 
as I take my eyes off you.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.250
Well, I mean, running dashes 
is super boring, you know?

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.660
And I'm always the fastest anyway.

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:50.590
Kabaddi. Kabaddi.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.680
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.430
His reach is insane!

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.350
When Takaya is raiding, you have to give up 
the bonus line and fall back, or else...

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:03.650
Nope, not doing this.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:04.100
Huh?

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:07.080
Rokugen-san, please, get in here.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.360
When they're this slow, 
it messes with my rhythm!

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:11.890
You little...

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:16.460
Since I can cant for three times as long 
as most people, it's already super easy.

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:15.860
Kabaddi...

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:17.850
We have a set rotation.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:21.090
This isn't any fun.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:22.690
And I mean, the thing is...

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:27.000
I came up on land with the excitement 
of a water creature evolving, you know?

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:30.150
This isn't like when you were a swimmer.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:32.000
This involves teamwork.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:37.260
But from the sounds you're making, 
Rokugen-san, I can tell you're excited.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.260
My self-control fails me.

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:45.470
That's natural. I mean, facing off against 
a powerful opponent is fun, isn't it?

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:47.770
It's boring when your opponent is weak.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.630
I'll switch out.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.650
I hate to say it, but he's the 
real thing in kabaddi, too.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.370
Here it comes.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:00.590
Guess I'd better dive in for real.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:14.310
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:10.720
This says he took first 
at nationals in swimming.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:16.170
<b>National Middle School Championship
Consecutive Wins</b>

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:16.170
<b>Takaya Ren</b>

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:16.170
<b>Comments on Winning</b>

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:12.790
He's a lot like Yoigoshi-kun.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:16.170
The way he's tall and came 
from a different sport...

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.930
I like Yoigoshi better.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:25.100
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:22.680
I don't know why he quit swimming 
and chose kabaddi, but...

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.100
Maybe he was looking for opponents?

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.320
Kabaddi!

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:30.530
Kabaddi...

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:27.790
You and me, Kei.

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:30.930
Let's compete to see who can accomplish 
the most in this next match.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:31.560
Compete?

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.380
That's right.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:37.200
Competing with you to see who can help 
our little juniors grow the most, Kei...

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.570
It's fun.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:41.820
You really are annoying.

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:43.580
There you go again.

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:48.080
Kabaddi! Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:46.370
Let me just say, no one beats me 
when it comes to training people.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:51.330
Blast it! One point again?

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.570
Man, he got me.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:55.650
Azemichi! Come here a sec.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:56.600
Sir!

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.680
Well, I guess I'll go make 
something of Yoigoshi-kun.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:09.060
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:06.630
A practice match?

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:07.530
When?

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:09.060
This weekend.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.140
We're playing one of the Kanto 
region's top four, Souwa High School.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.560
It'll be five-on-five.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.860
Kanto top four right off the bat, huh? 
Nice work getting that set up.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.420
I know their captain, you see.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:21.610
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:23.130
Are they strong?

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:34.130
<b>Strong and Steady</b>

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:26.790
Strong enough that when you think of 
kabaddi in Tokyo, you think of them.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.020
They've had a kabaddi team since before 
the tournament was established.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:33.630
They have a lot of members and many of 
them have fully developed physiques.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.620
They'd been in a bit of a slump lately,

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:40.230
but since Rokugen from the world team 
joined, they've gotten stronger again.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:44.140
They made it to the final four last year
 after their ace raider joined.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:47.850
It may be a practice match, but those 
two will definitely be playing.

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:55.600
It really is totally different!

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:57.110
It really is fun!

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:59.420
Hey, Rokugen-san!

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:02.110
Between me and this Ojo, 
which one is stronger?

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:04.360
Ojo.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.620
No hesitation.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:09.370
I'm eager to face him.

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:13.100
He's just gotten out of the hospital, 
so he'll probably be on the bench. 

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:15.080
If he does play, it'll probably 
only be in the final stages.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.750
Huh? But...

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:21.260
If we get forty points in the first half, 
he might come out earlier, right?

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.820
Okay, time for practice! 
Everyone, get on the court!

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.040
What're you taking a break for?

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.290
You told us to get out!

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:30.980
You're better than nothing.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.640
Okay. You're dead!

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:37.650
<i>He's inconsistent, but our 
beast isn't just talk.</i>

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:37.650
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.610
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:46.610
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:51.160
I'm planning to wolf down your team, Ojo.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.230
Do you have someone?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.420
A beast who can take us on?

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.460
Special training, huh? 
Our opponents must be pretty crazy.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:06.810
Yoigoshi-kun, you're going to wrestle with 
their ace raider, Takaya, and beat him.

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:09.840
On top of having the same kind 
of reach and speed as you,

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:16.350
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:13.480
he can keep up the cant for an unusually 
long time, giving him more time to raid.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.350
According to the data, it can be 
as much as a minute and a half.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:17.540
It's only one breath!

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:20.190
Usually, the cant only goes for 
about thirty seconds, right?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:24.070
He'll be calm and take his time to attack.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:27.450
Getting only one point 
per raid makes him antsy.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:31.960
Yoigoshi-kun, I'm going to teach you a 
whole bunch of techniques for scoring.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.710
Watch closely... and learn.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.200
Yes, sir!

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.880
We're the Noukin High School kabaddi team!

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.190
Thank you for having us!

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:47.630
Sure thing!

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.890
I'll show you to the locker rooms!

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:52.090
They only have six members?

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:54.640
But, one of them was on the 
world team with Captain Rokugen.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.610
Is that Ojo? He's so skinny.

00:13:57.610 --> 00:13:59.150
What's with the bald guy?

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:01.820
And they've got a really huge guy, too!

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.920
That's the soccer guy. 
"Unstoppable," they called him.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:04.630
Unstoppable?

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:06.160
He's famous!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.690
You really are amazing, you know that?

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.680
So, you've come, my friend.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.460
It's been a while, Rokugen!

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:20.780
Is that Souwa's captain? They seem 
like they get along pretty well.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.410
Is that how it looks?

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.780
Thanks for having us today.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:28.130
Huh?

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.650
Taking a break because 
of an injury? Pathetic.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:35.680
With a captain who can't even look after 
himself, I feel sorry for your team.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:39.220
We've got a lot of really capable 
guys on our team, you see.

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:42.690
Even if I'm not standing around arrogantly 
issuing commands, they won't slack off.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:45.270
The air is crackling over there.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:47.700
But my juniors' game sense is...

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.480
If we're talking about that, then mine are...

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:51.200
Stop bragging about your juniors.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.680
I'm sorry, but we'll be winning this.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.450
That'll be us.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.210
I'm glad to see you, too, Ojo's friend.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:09.900
<i>"Ojo's friend," is it?</i>

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.720
<b>Noukin Locker Room</b>

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.720
This is your locker room.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.220
Welcome!

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.580
T-Takaya-senpai?!

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.230
I'm here to pay my respects.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.300
<i>This is the guy?</i>

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:25.100
Please, come in!

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.080
You. You're the only one who's different.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:35.180
Are you a rookie?

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:41.560
And you with the shiny head, you are, 
too, right? You seem pretty hyped.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.850
Oh, what a nice sound.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:44.750
What're you doing?

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.500
And, the man in question is...

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:49.420
Huh? Oh!

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.940
Are you Ojo-san?

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:51.510
Yes.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.250
Nice to meet you!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.510
I was so excited to play you, 
I woke up extra early!

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:59.800
I'm sorry, but today I won't be...

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:01.770
Don't worry.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:05.770
I'll get us a huge point gap in 
the first half and drag you out.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:12.280
<b>Takaya Ren ♥</b>

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:12.280
<b>Takaya Ren Fan Club</b>

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:18.540
<b>Kabaddi for Beginners</b>

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:19.000
Coach, you can't have called off 
voluntary practice today because of...

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.990
I'm sorry. We're doing this to 
try to get Yoigoshi-kun to join!

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:24.920
What? Again?

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:27.260
Do not cause trouble for our opponents.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:29.920
I was just saying hello.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:34.210
He's an interesting one.

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:36.580
Would you usually say that stuff 
right in front of your opponents?

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:40.430
He's either really stupid, or it's 
a foregone conclusion for him.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:43.940
Everyone, please line up.

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:50.200
Th-The captain isn't lining up?

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.190
It's only the members 
playing that do it, right?

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:56.520
He's a rookie, isn't he?

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.700
He seems the most relaxed.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.790
Apparently, he's a fierce player who made 
it to the national final four in soccer.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:03.960
Huh? Why's he playing kabaddi?

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.580
I should be asking you that.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.050
Huh?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:11.260
I made it to number one in swimming, 
so I figured I was done.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:12.280
Stop it.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:15.850
But you didn't make it to 
number one, so why'd you quit?

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:20.180
We're ready to start.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.430
The first half will be twenty minutes.

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:24.260
Crossing the bonus line

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:26.690
when there are five or more defensemen 
will result in one point.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:29.160
Starting, we have white...

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:31.190
Souwa will start the match!

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:32.810
Let's have a good game!

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:36.450
<b>Kabaddi for Beginners</b>

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.220
Coach! What are the rules?

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.450
I'm looking them up right now!

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:39.700
They're starting! And it looks 
like they're holding hands!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:46.210
<b>Defense
Noukin 5 Players</b>

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:42.410
Yoigoshi, when we have 
an odd number on defense,

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.720
you don't need to be part of the chain.

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:45.520
Stay nimble and dodge them.

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.210
Got it!

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:50.210
<b>Raider
Souwa / Takaya</b>

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:49.690
I'm gonna nail it right off the bat, okay?

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:53.710
Don't let your guard down. They have 
a guy who's clearly well-built.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.300
<i>Are you coming for me, ace raider?</i>

00:17:56.710 --> 00:17:59.180
<i>He's about the same height as me, but...</i>

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:06.230
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:02.430
<i>he feels a lot bigger.</i>

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:06.230
<i>Guys, is this how you 
felt going up against me?</i>

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:12.610
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:12.610
What is that pose?

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:13.610
Kabaddi...

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.830
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:19.450
Kabaddi!

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:24.240
<i>Hey, you're pretty fast!</i>

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:26.960
Kabaddi.

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:34.000
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.630
Misumi got taken down?

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:38.880
Bonus line!

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:40.890
He'll take the point!

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:42.510
Bonus line?

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:47.520
It seems that if he crosses that line 
in the back, he gets another point.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.940
Really...

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:55.360
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:55.960 --> 00:19:03.170
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:00.060
He hasn't stopped the cant!

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:02.150
Misumi! Go stop his raid!

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.700
Souwa

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.700
Noukin

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.950
<b>Souwa</b>

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.950
<b>Noukin</b>

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:07.950
Oh, dear. Just two points?

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.960
Red numbers 3 and 5, out!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:14.960
<b>Noukin OUT
Misumi, Azemichi</b>

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:13.100
Sorry.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:14.960
Why'd he push him back just now?

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:15.290
We'll get the next one.

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:19.970
When the opponent tries to continue the raid, 
the guys who got touched push him out.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:28.470
Souwa

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:28.470
Noukin

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:23.850
It's so that their teammates who haven't 
been touched don't get targeted.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:26.030
They still seem to be talking basics.

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:29.250
What's with him? 
He's huge, but he's a rookie?

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:33.260
I see. So, the two who were 
touched leave the court.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:38.180
I'll go raid. You guys are so stiff,
 you won't be any match for them.

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:39.490
Who are you talking about?

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:43.120
If I get two points, 
you guys can come back, right?

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.370
Sorry your break's gonna be so short.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:49.370
He's so cool!

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:52.620
It's too early for <i>that</i> yet, Yoigoshi-kun.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.880
<b>Raider
Noukin / Yoigoshi</b>

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.880
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:57.630
Fall back!

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:00.010
<b>Defense
Souwa 5 Players</b>

00:19:57.950 --> 00:20:01.230
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.370
Don't force a tackle!

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:00.010
Sir!

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:01.880
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:04.990
You can say this about most sports,

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:07.510
but the thing you need most 
in a game is momentum.

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:09.520
If you can gain momentum,

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.570
it's easier to achieve miracles 
that exceed your abilities.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.870
Of course, you do risk failure,

00:20:15.870 --> 00:20:19.300
but he's always been a player who's 
good at creating momentum.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.550
He comes in pretty hard, but I 
don't feel like I can get him.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:25.210
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:25.210
Is it just a bluff so he can aim 
for the point from the bonus line?

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:28.030
Kabaddi...

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:29.740
We won't let you!

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.440
No matter the sport...

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:34.540
the importance of momentum doesn't change.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:36.650
Right?

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:48.800
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:50.140
Yoigoshi the Unstoppable.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:54.190
<i>I got three of them!</i>

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:57.260
A roll kick?

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.690
He was aiming for the defense 
to gather in one place!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:02.940
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:06.450
<i>Come on. Push me out.</i>

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:08.160
Kabaddi... Kabaddi...

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:09.200
Strong and Steady

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:09.200
<b>Souwa</b>

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:09.200
<b>Noukin</b>

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:12.690
<i>That was amazing. He made it 
seem like it was only natural.</i>

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.080
<i>But he only succeeded at that 
about once in ten times.</i>

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:17.810
Come on back, you scaredy cats.

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:19.960
Can't you just let me praise 
you for once, you numskull?

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:24.040
Things have gotten quite a bit easier.

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:26.580
You'd better show some gratitude.

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:29.170
That's right. If you work 
hard, things change.

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:29.720
Huh?

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.270
It's not a bluff anymore, right?

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:35.840
Your hat trick.

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:40.940
Let me show you my hat trick!

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:43.400
<b>Souwa</b>

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:43.400
<b>Noukin</b>

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:46.460
<i>A mere minute into the game...</i>

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:49.050
Is Noukin really a weak school?

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:51.590
He got three points without grabbing anyone!

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:54.540
<i>opinions all around had clearly changed.</i>

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:57.540
<i>Some had begun to see opponents 
as true challengers...</i>

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.630
<i>Some had made unforeseen mistakes,</i>

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.050
<i>and felt pressured by the 
achievements of their peers...</i>

00:22:02.930 --> 00:22:06.550
<i>Every gaze in the venue was 
focused on a single rookie...</i>

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:10.430
He doesn't waver at all.

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:12.750
<i>...except for one.</i>

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:18.440
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"Chase X Counterattack"</b>

00:23:49.410 --> 00:23:52.570
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:52.570
Next time... "Chase X Counterattack!"

00:23:52.570 --> 00:23:53.290
Kabaddi!
